<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>News Releases - NVIDIA Newsroom</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com</link><description>All News</description><language>en-us</language><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:50:14 GMT</pubDate><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:50:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>iPressroom</generator><item><title>Volvo Cars and NVIDIA Expand Partnership to Advance Safe Automated Driving</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/volvo-cars-and-nvidia-expand-partnership-to-advance-safe-automated-driving</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/e517972ce6ea647b2c088652f4a6c47c/6ad111e43d63320c839b1aba_JHH-Volvo-1600x900/JHH-Volvo-1600x900_thmb.jpg?v=8bb5a42f-7901-4d4b-b581-3e273067984b" fileSize="1208579" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/e517972ce6ea647b2c088652f4a6c47c/6ad111e43d63320c839b1aba_JHH-Volvo-1600x900/JHH-Volvo-1600x900_thmb.jpg?v=8bb5a42f-7901-4d4b-b581-3e273067984b" alt="NVIDIA and Volvo" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Volvo Cars today announced it is expanding its partnership with NVIDIA to unlock new levels of safety in automated driving technology in future cars from Volvo, building on the companies&amp;rsquo; decade-long collaboration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Guided by Volvo Cars&amp;rsquo; pioneering safety knowledge and powered by the NVIDIA Hyperion sensor and compute architecture, the technology will enable future Volvo cars to safely navigate complex real-world environments from door to door. This includes everything from highways and busy urban streets to parking scenarios.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;The technology will make its debut in a next-generation Volvo car as part of the company&amp;rsquo;s recently announced largest-ever product push.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Volvo Cars will combine its industry-leading vehicle safety systems and engineering expertise with NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s AI and accelerated computing technologies. These include the Hyperion sensor and compute architecture, Halos OS, and Alpamayo Stack driving software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Together, the companies will raise the bar for AI-enabled car safety while making driving feel easier and more effortless for customers, with a gradual introduction of eyes-off and mind-off driving.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Volvo Cars brings nearly a century of real-world safety research and its human-centric approach to this development. The ambition is to set a new benchmark for automated driving that is safe, convenient and worthy of customer trust.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Volvo has been synonymous with car safety for almost 100 years,&amp;rdquo; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;said H&amp;aring;kan Samuelsson, president and CEO of Volvo Cars.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; &amp;ldquo;By working with NVIDIA, we bring together two distinct strengths: industry-leading safety knowledge and world-class AI technology. That combination gives us a unique opportunity to create safer and more attractive cars for our customers.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Accelerated computing has transformed the car into an intelligent machine that can understand the world around it,&amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Volvo has spent nearly a century protecting people on the road. Together, we&amp;rsquo;re combining Volvo&amp;rsquo;s extraordinary vehicle safety systems with NVIDIA Hyperion and Halos to build a new generation of cars that make driving safer and more effortless.&amp;rdquo;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-2de20e7a-7fff-4ecd-3a41-4921901af3d2"&gt;&lt;span&gt;This expanded partnership marks another milestone in the companies&amp;rsquo; long-standing collaboration, which began in 2017. Volvo Cars is bringing the industry&amp;rsquo;s most advanced computing capabilities into its next generation of electric cars, establishing it as a leader in software-defined cars.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category><category>Driving</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:54:08 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Volvo Cars today announced it is expanding its partnership with NVIDIA to unlock new levels of safety in automated driving technology in future cars from Volvo, building on the companies’ decade-long collaboration.

]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/e517972ce6ea647b2c088652f4a6c47c/JHH-Volvo-1600x900.jpg" length="1208579" type="image/jpeg"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/volvo-cars-and-nvidia-expand-partnership-to-advance-safe-automated-driving</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:30:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Be There for the Beginning: Celebrate the Launch of NVIDIA RTX Spark</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-launch-event-invite/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/e5eef2a45338109b7e6d80237afb8d8e/6ad1069d3d6332e50ab73366_press-nvidia-rtx-spark-launch-events-1920x1080-1-842x450/press-nvidia-rtx-spark-launch-events-1920x1080-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=d37e4c6c-59d0-463b-b352-9fc43a08dc9c" fileSize="217794" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/e5eef2a45338109b7e6d80237afb8d8e/6ad1069d3d6332e50ab73366_press-nvidia-rtx-spark-launch-events-1920x1080-1-842x450/press-nvidia-rtx-spark-launch-events-1920x1080-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=d37e4c6c-59d0-463b-b352-9fc43a08dc9c" alt="press-nvidia-rtx-spark-launch-events-1920x1080-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:00:18 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[A new beginning for Windows PCs starts tomorrow with the launch of NVIDIA RTX Spark — one PC built for creators, gamers and AI agents. All are invited to celebrate with NVIDIA and partners at launch events around the world. Share Your Spark Every PC has a story. What was your first Windows PC, and […]]]></description><author>Shreevar Rastogi</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-launch-event-invite/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:00:23 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Adobe and NVIDIA Expand Collaboration to Speed Agentic Creation</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/adobe-and-nvidia-expand-collaboration-to-speed-agentic-creation</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/dc41fbe271cc85f622d85087141e98fd/6ad031583d63327ade3da8c2_adobe-and-nvidia/adobe-and-nvidia_thmb.png?v=e30ad072-7cc9-43cd-8488-653fe16935c5" fileSize="91749" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/dc41fbe271cc85f622d85087141e98fd/6ad031583d63327ade3da8c2_adobe-and-nvidia/adobe-and-nvidia_thmb.png?v=e30ad072-7cc9-43cd-8488-653fe16935c5" alt="Adobe and NVIDIA" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-f0d2a6af-7fff-191f-6272-d952127084ff"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li role="presentation"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-afb59be3-7fff-c339-958e-135b78aacee5"&gt;Adobe is expanding its collaboration with NVIDIA to optimize its flagship tools including Adobe Photoshop, Premiere, Substance 3D, Frame.io and Brand Concierge, delivering faster AI-powered creation, production and personalization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li role="presentation"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-afb59be3-7fff-c339-958e-135b78aacee5"&gt;Adobe is bringing the power of the NVIDIA RTX Spark superchip to its agentic creative applications Photoshop, Premiere and Substance 3D. Optimized to take full advantage of RTX Spark, these applications deliver up to 2x faster AI processing, editing, color and effects, helping creatives iterate faster and stay in their creative flow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li role="presentation"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-afb59be3-7fff-c339-958e-135b78aacee5"&gt;Adobe Brand Concierge is now optimized with NVIDIA Nemotron open models, providing enterprises a flexible and efficient way to deliver high-quality conversational experiences at scale, with NVIDIA also selecting Brand Concierge to power relevant and contextual customer interactions on NVIDIA.com.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adobe (Nasdaq: ADBE), the global technology leader that unleashes creativity, productivity and customer experiences through innovative tools and platforms, and NVIDIA today announced an expansion of their partnership to optimize Adobe&amp;rsquo;s flagship tools including Adobe Photoshop, Premiere, Substance 3D, Frame.io and Brand Concierge, delivering faster AI-powered creation, production and personalization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;This work builds on Adobe and NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s strategic partnership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://news.adobe.com/news/2026/03/adobe-and-nvidia-announce-strategic-partnership"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;announced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt; in March, which brings together Adobe&amp;rsquo;s creative and marketing workflows, models and technology with NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s open models, libraries, research and accelerated computing to accelerate creative, production and marketing workflows across video, images, 3D and other creative media. That collaboration includes GPU acceleration for media ingestion and intelligence in Frame.io, as well as ongoing work around Adobe Substance 3D, Adobe Firefly Foundry and 3D digital twin workflows for enterprise customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Creative workflows are more multimodal than ever, with many projects spanning images, video, audio, motion and 3D, making performance critical to helping creatives stay focused on their ideas and craft,&amp;rdquo; said Deepa Subramaniam, vice president, product marketing, creative professionals, Adobe. &amp;ldquo;By partnering with NVIDIA to optimize Photoshop, Premiere and Substance 3D for RTX Spark and accelerating Frame.io in the cloud, we&amp;rsquo;re delivering the performance creatives need to bring their ideas to life.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;ldquo;AI agents are helping creators unlock deeper and richer workflows using the Adobe applications they know and love,&amp;rdquo; said Jason Paul, vice president, local AI, NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;Powered by RTX Spark, Adobe&amp;rsquo;s optimized tools deliver up to 2x faster performance to accelerate these new workflows.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empowering Creatives With Faster Adobe Tools Rearchitected With NVIDIA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Creative professionals today move between image, video, motion and 3D, sometimes all within the same project. As AI increasingly becomes part of the creative process, they need technology that keeps pace with the speed of their ideas and the complexity of their workflows. As an industry leader in creativity, Adobe&amp;rsquo;s tools apply decades of creative expertise to amplify human potential and make it easier to quickly turn ideas into impactful work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Adobe is bringing the power of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/products/rtx-spark/"&gt;&lt;span&gt;NVIDIA RTX Spark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt; superchip, launching tomorrow, Oct. 16, to its agentic creative applications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.adobe.com/products/photoshop/landpa.html?sdid=NC5FRF5H&amp;amp;mv=search&amp;amp;mv2=paidsearch&amp;amp;ef_id=CjwKCAjw25fWBhAVEiwAMopNjstHDT19mM-5LkWVmBIcDAczQqnSqGVOUSLwPjsG4LgbGEQu5WMpGBoCJK8QAvD_BwE:G:s&amp;amp;s_kwcid=AL!3085!3!714745362176!e!!g!!adobe%20photoshop!1712238394!67643541820&amp;amp;mv=search&amp;amp;gad_source=1&amp;amp;gad_campaignid=1712238394&amp;amp;gbraid=0AAAAAD5r4Ax04lbW1NyPBSSOCfy24Op8k&amp;amp;gclid=CjwKCAjw25fWBhAVEiwAMopNjstHDT19mM-5LkWVmBIcDAczQqnSqGVOUSLwPjsG4LgbGEQu5WMpGBoCJK8QAvD_BwE"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Photoshop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.adobe.com/products/premiere/campaign/pricing.html?sdid=SYBNLTYL&amp;amp;mv=search&amp;amp;mv2=paidsearch&amp;amp;ef_id=CjwKCAjw25fWBhAVEiwAMopNjtcLMN2AcWMBv8xYnWPlfc8e8VDNoMNMv42TQ9mJ_jYmxCFuOrvOwxoCpOQQAvD_BwE:G:s&amp;amp;s_kwcid=AL!3085!3!700626653693!e!!g!!adobe%20premiere!1712852043!83993219448&amp;amp;mv=search&amp;amp;gad_source=1&amp;amp;gad_campaignid=1712852043&amp;amp;gbraid=0AAAAAD5r4AzW_Ywl4aZuTRdUZLKUPNGlx&amp;amp;gclid=CjwKCAjw25fWBhAVEiwAMopNjtcLMN2AcWMBv8xYnWPlfc8e8VDNoMNMv42TQ9mJ_jYmxCFuOrvOwxoCpOQQAvD_BwE"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Premiere&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt; and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.adobe.com/creativecloud/3d-ar/campaign/pricing.html?sdid=DRCF12SK&amp;amp;mv=search&amp;amp;mv2=paidsearch&amp;amp;gad_source=1&amp;amp;gad_campaignid=24204287413&amp;amp;gbraid=0AAAAADraYsIwwWoO4Of28kjfP-txCwPuT&amp;amp;gclid=CjwKCAjw25fWBhAVEiwAMopNjrlq2fTH3nQYYNHWXj4T1z5ZhIxFXmzU8CVFDjeiRGiPvUJzJEsMMRoCsXEQAvD_BwE"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Substance 3D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;. RTX-accelerated and optimized to take full advantage of RTX Spark&amp;rsquo;s unified memory and AI compute, these applications deliver up to 2x faster AI processing, editing, color and effects, helping creatives iterate faster and stay in their creative flow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Adobe rearchitected Photoshop around GPU-accelerated compositing to be faster and more responsive for creative tasks from removing distractions with the Remove Tool to applying effects like Gaussian Blur and Light Leaks directly on canvas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Some of the most demanding post-production workflows in Premiere, from playback and rendering to effects, color and AI-powered tools, are RTX-accelerated and optimized for RTX Spark. This results in real, tangible speed gains for popular audio and video features in Premiere like Enhance Speech and Object Mask. For 3D artists using Substance 3D Painter, RTX Spark speeds up the heaviest steps around texturing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerating Cloud Video Workflows With Frame.io and NVIDIA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Adobe is also using NVIDIA accelerated computing to speed cloud media processing and intelligent content discovery for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://frame.io/creative-cloud"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Adobe Frame.io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;, helping production teams find and use growing media libraries faster. The updated Frame.io pipeline uses NVIDIA video acceleration, including NVIDIA NVDEC for hardware-accelerated decoding and NVIDIA TensorRT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;trade;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; with CUDA&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;for content preprocessing and embedding generation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Moving compute-intensive video decoding, preprocessing and embedding generation onto NVIDIA GPUs lets Frame.io process media faster and make it searchable sooner, while supporting more responsive discovery across large content libraries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Early performance results from selected Frame.io transcode and search workloads show:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Approximately 5x faster embedding generation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;4-5x improvement in P95 processing latency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;An approximately 80% smaller search proxy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;For creative teams, these gains mean uploaded content becomes searchable sooner, larger libraries refresh more efficiently, and discovery and review stay frictionless as media volumes grow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;Personalized Conversational Experiences With Adobe Brand Concierge Optimized on NVIDIA Nemotron&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Brands also want more choice and value from the AI models powering personalized experiences. Open models can help meet that need, providing a flexible and efficient way to deliver high-quality, responsive conversations at enterprise scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Adobe and NVIDIA worked together to optimize Brand Concierge using &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/foundation-models/nemotron/"&gt;&lt;span&gt;NVIDIA Nemotron&amp;trade;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt; open models. This version will be available to enterprise customers later this year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;NVIDIA has also selected Brand Concierge to drive personalized conversational experiences grounded in organizational data and content. This enables NVIDIA to tailor interactions on their website based on customer needs, while leveraging Nemotron to deliver fast, high-quality responses at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Sparking Creativity, to the MAX&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-e2075af0-7fff-4d21-81e7-3832b767d179"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Get ready for what&amp;rsquo;s next &amp;mdash; with three days of creative skill-building, visionary keynotes and valuable connections at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://max.adobe.com/"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Adobe MAX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span&gt;, running Nov. 10-12. Adobe and NVIDIA will showcase the latest advancements for creators alongside their hardware partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span id="docs-internal-guid-f0d2a6af-7fff-191f-6272-d952127084ff"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category><category>Content Creation / Rendering</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:01:34 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Adobe (Nasdaq: ADBE), the global technology leader that unleashes creativity, productivity and customer experiences through innovative tools and platforms, and NVIDIA today announced an expansion of their partnership to optimize Adobe’s flagship tools including Adobe Photoshop, Premiere, Substance 3D, Frame.io and Brand Concierge, delivering faster AI-powered creation, production and personalization.]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/dc41fbe271cc85f622d85087141e98fd/adobe-and-nvidia.png" length="91749" type="image/png"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/adobe-and-nvidia-expand-collaboration-to-speed-agentic-creation</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Open From Data Center to Desktop: NVIDIA Expands Nemotron Family With Highest Efficiency Super VL and Bolt Models</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nemotron-3-5-super-vl/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/1537766779024a2b34767af63823c4c6/6ad0ea933d633256e451ff7c_FIRST-agentic-ai-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-blog-1920x1080-5783765-842x450/FIRST-agentic-ai-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-blog-1920x1080-5783765-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=fdd21978-126e-4822-81aa-d850892d3765" fileSize="38269" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/1537766779024a2b34767af63823c4c6/6ad0ea933d633256e451ff7c_FIRST-agentic-ai-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-blog-1920x1080-5783765-842x450/FIRST-agentic-ai-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-blog-1920x1080-5783765-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=fdd21978-126e-4822-81aa-d850892d3765" alt="FIRST-agentic-ai-nemotron-3.5-super-vl-blog-1920x1080-5783765-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:00:39 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today released Nemotron 3.5 Super VL, an open 120-billion-parameter model that delivers the fastest task completion and highest accuracy for specialized always-on agents. Joining it are two new edge models: Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B-A9B 24GB, optimized to balance intelligence and speed per GB for local agentic workloads, and Nemotron 3.5 Bolt E4B 4GB, optimized […]]]></description><author>Kari Briski</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nemotron-3-5-super-vl/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:00:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Dial Up the Cloud: NVIDIA DLSS 4.5 Controls Arrive on GeForce NOW</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-enshrouded-update/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/677e6e6ccaa38ca91f968724d2a6579b/6ad0ce993d6332cc8ac0808c_GFN_Thursday_October_15_2026-842x450/GFN_Thursday_October_15_2026-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=edf71b41-f2fb-482c-a0cb-b89b1b58e5b2" fileSize="82284" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/677e6e6ccaa38ca91f968724d2a6579b/6ad0ce993d6332cc8ac0808c_GFN_Thursday_October_15_2026-842x450/GFN_Thursday_October_15_2026-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=edf71b41-f2fb-482c-a0cb-b89b1b58e5b2" alt="GFN_Thursday_October_15_2026-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:01:18 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Dial in the next gaming session this GFN Thursday. New NVIDIA DLSS 4.5 controls give GeForce NOW members more choice over how supported games look and perform in the cloud, even without the latest hardware. Then, step into the Shroud as Keen Games’ Enshrouded leaves early access with its 1.0 release, or let the bolts […]]]></description><author>GeForce NOW Community</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-enshrouded-update/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:00:59 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Expands Advanced Technology Access for Europe’s Scientific Community Through Open Learning Resources, Collaborations and Compute</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ec-scientific-computing-pledge/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/63c5c6f840f033af6624e1983001d020/6ad0a4813d6332fd5ce8e34e_ai-in-science-enablers-1920x1080-1-842x450/ai-in-science-enablers-1920x1080-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=88967496-5156-4b07-9365-dcacfb347762" fileSize="61426" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/63c5c6f840f033af6624e1983001d020/6ad0a4813d6332fd5ce8e34e_ai-in-science-enablers-1920x1080-1-842x450/ai-in-science-enablers-1920x1080-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=88967496-5156-4b07-9365-dcacfb347762" alt="ai-in-science-enablers-1920x1080-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:01:41 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Much of today’s scientific progress begins with computation.  But turning accelerated computing’s potential into scientific progress — modeling climate systems, designing molecules, simulating materials and more — depends on more than breakthrough technology. Especially for smaller labs, early-career scientists or science-based startups, the hardest part of research can be everything that comes before the science: […]]]></description><author>Rod Evans</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ec-scientific-computing-pledge/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:00:12 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>The Nordics and NVIDIA Show What’s Possible When a Region Commits to Advanced Computing</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nordics-technology-ecosystem/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/d11dc853704dbe0c7dafb78271a1f720/6ad05e303d633281a2481569_nordics-embrace-social-1920x1080-5822300-842x450/nordics-embrace-social-1920x1080-5822300-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=d81f8fb1-1e93-4113-a222-f03f5d62f3d3" fileSize="31588" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/d11dc853704dbe0c7dafb78271a1f720/6ad05e303d633281a2481569_nordics-embrace-social-1920x1080-5822300-842x450/nordics-embrace-social-1920x1080-5822300-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=d81f8fb1-1e93-4113-a222-f03f5d62f3d3" alt="nordics-embrace-social-1920x1080-5822300-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:01:40 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[The Nordic countries have become the European leader in unicorn startup density, producing the most emerging companies valued at $1 billion or more per capita on the continent. Now, a new chapter for the region is unfolding as countries race to build one of Europe’s most consequential technology ecosystems. The many computing advancements already underway […]]]></description><author>Linda Malm</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nordics-technology-ecosystem/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:00:12 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA and Semiconductor Leaders Advance AI Across Chip Design and Manufacturing for AI-Defined Fabs</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders-advance-ai-across-chip-design-and-manufacturing-for-ai-defined-labs</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/91e4671418fd42dd611fce974f821286/6aceab1a3d6332051d5dc521_nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders/nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders_thmb.jpg?v=5ac54765-981c-4c26-b6c2-cdd8daa42e94" fileSize="4987410" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/91e4671418fd42dd611fce974f821286/6aceab1a3d6332051d5dc521_nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders/nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders_thmb.jpg?v=5ac54765-981c-4c26-b6c2-cdd8daa42e94" alt="NVIDIA and Semiconductor Leaders Advance AI-Defined Fabs" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type="disc"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NVIDIA introduces cuPotential, a new NVIDIA CUDA-X library developers can use to build AI agents that simulate how atoms and molecules interact, accelerating already GPU-optimized workflows by an additional 2-3x in early-access testing.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NanoVDB, an open source library for working with 3D data, accelerates chipmaking simulation for AI-defined fabs, helping Lam Research achieve 30x faster simulation.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NVIDIA NPP, a library for processing images on GPUs, accelerates chipmaking inspection for AI-defined fabs, helping KLA accelerate inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Applied Materials, Cadence, KLA, Lam Research, Siemens, Synopsys and other semiconductor leaders are using NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s accelerated computing and AI stack across chip design, manufacturing and testing, helping drive faster development, better yield and greater production capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA today announced semiconductor leaders are adopting &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/technologies/cuda-x/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA CUDA-X&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;trade; libraries &amp;mdash; including the new NVIDIA cuPotential library, which developers can use to build AI agents that simulate how atoms and molecules interact &amp;mdash; to advance AI-defined fabs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI-defined fabs are semiconductor factories where AI helps engineers optimize processes, solve production issues and improve production efficiency. As demand for advanced chips rises, such fabs must expand production while managing increasingly complex manufacturing processes. Engineers need new ways to model materials, analyze inspection data and test process changes in digital twins before applying them in production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The expanded CUDA-X portfolio gives AI agents and engineering applications accelerated tools for semiconductor simulation, 3D data processing and image analysis, helping automate more engineering work across chip design and manufacturing so fabs can predict process behavior and improve yield.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;The semiconductor industry made the AI revolution possible. Now, AI is transforming how chips are built,&amp;rdquo; said Tim Costa, vice president and general manager of industrial and computational engineering at NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;As fabs race to meet demand for advanced chips, NVIDIA CUDA-X and Omniverse libraries give AI agents accelerated simulation and inspection tools to help engineers manage complexity, improve yield and advance AI-defined fabs.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVIDIA cuPotential Accelerates How Researchers Model Atomic Interactions &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Understanding how atoms and molecules interact is critical to modeling semiconductor materials and manufacturing processes, but these calculations can take significant amounts of time, even in software already optimized for GPUs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA cuPotential accelerates atomic-scale simulation with specialized GPU-accelerated functions developers can add to existing software. It helps researchers model electrical forces and other interactions across large numbers of atoms to test and refine simulations faster. Synopsys is among the early adopters using cuPotential to accelerate materials simulations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By making these modeling capabilities available to AI agents, cuPotential helps agents run, evaluate and iterate on advanced molecular simulations. In early-access testing, the library accelerated already GPU-optimized workflows by an additional 2-3x.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Semiconductor Leaders Advance AI-Defined Fabs With NVIDIA CUDA-X&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
AI-defined fabs require faster ways to model chip designs, materials behavior and manufacturing processes before changes reach production. NVIDIA CUDA-X libraries &amp;mdash; including NVIDIA cuPotential for simulating atomic interactions, NVIDIA cuEST for modeling electronic behavior and NVIDIA cuDSS for solving complex engineering simulations &amp;mdash; accelerate these workloads to help make fabs more autonomous.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Synopsys is using cuPotential, cuEST and cuDSS to accelerate semiconductor simulations, with early QuantumATK results showing a potential 30x speedup using cuEST, and S-Device benchmarks showing a 12x speedup using cuDSS. The company&amp;rsquo;s AgentEngineer solutions interoperate with &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/foundation-models/nemotron/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Nemotron&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;trade; open models and &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/nemo/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA NeMo&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;trade; to support AI agents for chip design and verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cadence is using NVIDIA accelerated computing, NVIDIA Nemotron open models and CUDA-X libraries to bring agentic AI to the design and simulation of electromechanical systems &amp;mdash; from semiconductors to advanced packaging and printed circuit boards. Examples include Cadence AuraStack AI Super Agent optimizing advanced packages for heat and stress 8x faster using cuDSS with Cadence Celsius, and Nemotron with ChipStack AI Super Agent for semiconductor design and verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;COMSOL is accelerating semiconductor multiphysics simulations with NVIDIA cuDSS, delivering up to 10x faster simulations to help engineers optimize equipment and processes. Its upcoming COMSOL MCP Server will use the NVIDIA Nemotron Ultra open model to enable AI-assisted modeling and design exploration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Voltai accelerates advanced chip packaging with Voltaire, its agentic multiphysics platform for 3D-IC design and simulation. Voltaire combines AI agents with GPU-accelerated solvers powered by NVIDIA cuDSS and CUDA-X libraries, compressing complex electro-thermal-mechanical simulation workflows from months to a day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ChipAgents uses NVIDIA AI infrastructure and NVIDIA model-training and optimization software to develop specialized AI models for chip design. The company is also working with NVIDIA to develop &lt;a href="https://chipagents.ai/newsroom/chipagents-nvidia-build-a-chip-bench" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Build-A-Chip Bench&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, a new AI benchmark that evaluates agents across end-to-end workflows from specification to graphic data system. The benchmark gives the industry a comprehensive measure of progress toward fully autonomous semiconductor engineering.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVIDIA Open Libraries Help Prepare and Optimize Manufacturing Workflows&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Fabs depend on thousands of process steps that must be modeled, refined and validated before production. The &lt;a href="https://developer.nvidia.com/culitho" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA cuLitho&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; library accelerates calculations for printing chip patterns; NanoVDB &amp;mdash; an open source library for working with 3D data &amp;mdash; accelerates chipmaking simulations; and the open &lt;a href="https://developer.nvidia.com/physicsnemo" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA PhysicsNeMo&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;trade; framework helps train physics AI models to predict how physical systems behave.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://news.siemens.com/en-us/siemens-nvidia-culitho/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Siemens&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is using cuLitho to speed up Calibre software for chip-pattern refinement and mask preparation. Its Solido team is also developing agent-driven characterization workflows with Nemotron open models and &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/nemo/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA NeMo&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; open libraries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lam Research intends to integrate NanoVDB into its advanced semiconductor process modeling platform &lt;a href="https://www.lamresearch.com/product/semulator3d/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;SEMulator3D&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, part of the company&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href="https://www.lamresearch.com/semiverse-solutions/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Semiverse Solutions&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; family of virtual products. The addition of NanoVDB is expected to accelerate select wafer-etch modeling by up to 30x, while using NVIDIA PhysicsNeMo has been demonstrated to assist in reducing plasma-prediction simulation time to as little as milliseconds instead of days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Luminary is applying NVIDIA PhysicsNeMo to semiconductor package design, training physics AI models to predict temperature, pressure drop and thermal stress across package configurations &amp;mdash; enabling engineers to explore 100x more designs in the same schedule without running a new simulation for every option.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Defined Fabs Inspect and Test Chips With NVIDIA CUDA-X Libraries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
AI-defined fabs need to analyze inspection images and test data quickly enough to catch defects, maintain equipment and improve yield. NVIDIA NPP, a library for processing images on GPUs, and NVIDIA RAPIDS cuDF, a library for processing large datasets on GPUs, help accelerate test and quality-control workflows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using NVIDIA AI and accelerated computing, imec is removing noise from scanning electron microscope images used for sub-nanometer chip measurements and using NVIDIA cuLitho to enable computationally intensive process-window optical proximity correction &amp;mdash; achieving a 30% improvement in the lithography process window.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;KLA applied insights from its highly optimized production kernels to a new NPP NCC kernel that achieved performance levels 50x faster than earlier CPU versions, comparable with KLA&amp;rsquo;s hand-tuned implementations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Teradyne is using NVIDIA NPP and accelerated computing to accelerate image-sensor testing, and RAPIDS cuDF and CuPy for GPU calculations, to deliver approximately 85x faster probe-maintenance inference, helping identify degrading probes before they affect yield.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Advantest has integrated NVIDIA Nemotron and &lt;a href="https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Kumo-Anomaly" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Kumo-Anomaly&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; into ACS RTDI to enable AI-driven semiconductor production analytics. Powered by &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/data-center/technologies/blackwell-architecture/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Grace Blackwell &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;systems, ACS delivers real-time diagnostics and inferencing that recommend corrective actions for test cells. Advantest is also using &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/nemo/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA NeMo&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Switchyard AI agents to automate model selection, streamline semiconductor test workflows and reduce response times from hours to minutes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVIDIA Technologies Advance Fab Operations and Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
In an AI-defined fab, equipment data must move from instruments into AI systems fast enough to support operational decisions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Applied Materials is using NVIDIA Omniverse&amp;trade; and NVIDIA CUDA-X libraries, including cuDSS, cuEST and PhysicsNeMo, across materials discovery, process development and fab optimization &amp;mdash; enabling up to 35x faster chamber simulations and fab digital twins that help optimize layouts and material flow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Analog Devices Inc. is combining Synopsys physics simulation with the NVIDIA Isaac Sim&amp;trade; framework and Omniverse libraries to develop high-fidelity sensing simulations and robotic benchmarks, helping engineers evaluate how sensors behave within complete robotic systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FANUC and Foxconn are connecting their robot models to the Mega NVIDIA Omniverse Blueprint, enabling manufacturers to simulate and validate robotic operations in factory digital twins before physical deployment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OMRON is using NVIDIA Cosmos&amp;trade; open world models and the NVIDIA Metropolis Blueprint for video search and summarization in its inspection equipment to develop agents that combine visual data, equipment documentation and manufacturing knowledge. These agents help engineers analyze printed circuit board results, investigate potential defect causes, and support troubleshooting and quality control.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Availability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
NVIDIA cuPotential is available in early access. NanoVDB is available as open source within OpenVDB, and NPP is available through &lt;a href="https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda/toolkit" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Lam Research&amp;rsquo;s NanoVDB-accelerated SEMulator3D capability is targeted for release by the end of this year.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Learn more by joining &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/events/semicon-west/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA at SEMICON West&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:16:44 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today announced semiconductor leaders are adopting NVIDIA CUDA-X™ libraries — including the new NVIDIA cuPotential library, which developers can use to build AI agents that simulate how atoms and molecules interact — to advance AI-defined fabs.]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/91e4671418fd42dd611fce974f821286/nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders.jpg" length="4987410" type="image/jpeg"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-and-semiconductor-leaders-advance-ai-across-chip-design-and-manufacturing-for-ai-defined-labs</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:10:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>From Enterprise to Earthshot: UK’s Ecosystem Moves From Ambition to Application With NVIDIA</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/uk-ecosystem-deployment/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/1af23f952ae234850928e304df2a723d/6acf1b663d63323a5bda7ff4_uk-ecosystem-industries-842x450/uk-ecosystem-industries-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=6e353cb1-d85d-4289-b5bc-338799d77208" fileSize="641839" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/1af23f952ae234850928e304df2a723d/6acf1b663d63323a5bda7ff4_uk-ecosystem-industries-842x450/uk-ecosystem-industries-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=6e353cb1-d85d-4289-b5bc-338799d77208" alt="uk-ecosystem-industries-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:04:28 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Across industries, the U.K. is putting the full stack to work — and the scale of deployment is growing fast, from enterprises transforming their businesses to startups solving some of the planet’s hardest problems. NVIDIA is putting that principle into practice, including through a five-year, $250 million compute commitment to strengthen the U.K.’s agentic safety […]]]></description><author>Anthony Hills</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/uk-ecosystem-deployment/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:04:15 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Commits $250 Million to Advance UK Agentic Safety and Security Research Over the Next Five Years</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-commits-250-million-to-advance-uk-agentic-safety-and-security-research-over-the-next-five-years</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" fileSize="5094489" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" alt="NVIDIA Voyager" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type="disc"&gt;
	&lt;li style="text-align:left;"&gt;NVIDIA announces a compute donation valued at $250 million over five years to support U.K. agentic safety and security research.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li style="text-align:left;"&gt;The program will support the wider U.K. research community, with a proportion of the commitment supporting BOLD, SOFAIR and Imperial College London across fundamental agentic foundation models and robotics safety.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-bottom:6pt; text-align:left;"&gt;Compute access will be delivered through U.K.-based NVIDIA Cloud Partners, supporting the nation&amp;rsquo;s research capability and compute ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;NVIDIA today announced a five-year compute donation valued at $250 million to strengthen the United Kingdom&amp;rsquo;s agentic safety and security research capability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;The commitment will provide $50 million in compute access annually to support agentic safety and security research across the U.K. The majority will support the wider U.K. AI safety and security research community, with a proportion supporting work with the British Open-Ended Learning and Discovery Lab (BOLD), the Science of Fundamental AI Research Lab (SOFAIR) and Imperial College London.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;AI capability and safety must advance together,&amp;rdquo; said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;The U.K. brings world-class scientific rigor to this essential engineering challenge. With this $250 million commitment, NVIDIA will put accelerated computing in the hands of U.K. researchers to develop, test and strengthen safeguards for increasingly powerful AI. This is how the U.K. turns research leadership into real-world solutions &amp;mdash; and scientific progress into a future that benefits everyone.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;This commitment is a vote of confidence in our world-leading strength and expertise in AI research &amp;mdash; and, in particular, frontier AI safety that is becoming ever more important as AI&amp;rsquo;s capabilities develop,&amp;rdquo; said U.K. AI Minister Kanishka Narayan. &amp;ldquo;NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s donation will help Britain&amp;rsquo;s AI innovators access the resources they need to bring their ideas to life &amp;mdash; and, in the process, help build a distinctly British AI future that is safe, secure and that serves people&amp;rsquo;s best interests, objectives that will be central to the U.K.&amp;rsquo;s G20 presidency.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;To realise the opportunities of AI, people need to feel the technology is safe and secure. The government is committed to ensuring AI can be securely harnessed to fuel new discoveries and drive growth,&amp;ldquo; said U.K. Business Secretary Jonathan Reynolds.&amp;nbsp;&amp;ldquo;NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s investment will help British researchers continue to lead the world in that effort &amp;mdash; accelerating the breakthroughs that build trust and help us deploy AI safely.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthening UK Leadership in Agentic Safety and Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Compute provided through the initiative will be dedicated to agentic safety and security research.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;The program will connect complementary areas of U.K. research, including in AI safety and security. BOLD, led by the University of Oxford, is developing approaches that help AI systems learn, adapt and operate alongside people. SOFAIR, led by UCL, is exploring new open source AI architectures and more accessible ways to develop and deploy AI. Imperial&amp;rsquo;s work will include safety engineering and robotics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;We are experiencing a critical moment where AI safety as an afterthought is no longer appropriate for the open-ended, evolving world,&amp;rdquo; said Jakob Foerster, founding director of BOLD. &amp;ldquo;This compute will help us explore transparent and human-centric approaches to AI that allow us to collectively rise to the challenge by building in governance and human-AI co-improvement from the ground up.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;&amp;ldquo;The next frontier of artificial intelligence is physical &amp;mdash; robots, autonomous systems of agents that perceive, reason and act in the real world,&amp;rdquo; said Alessandra Russo, director of Imperial Frontier AI Research Lab and convening co-director of Human and AI, School of Convergence Science. &amp;ldquo;With NVIDIA and our industry partners, Imperial is working to ensure that safety and assurance is at the heart of this revolution, ensuring the U.K. leads not only in developing physical AI but in making it trustworthy for the communities and industries that will depend on it.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;NVIDIA will fund compute access through U.K.-based &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/data-center/gpu-cloud-computing/partners/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Cloud Partners&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, with infrastructure hosted in the U.K. This will support the U.K. compute ecosystem and provide a domestic platform for research. Provider selection, technical architecture and commercial terms are to be agreed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;As part of the wider initiative, research programs will focus on secure agents, open-model security and real-world threat mitigations. The work will support secure sandboxes, reproducible research and safety assessment benchmarks, including research conducted using &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai/openshell/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA OpenShell&amp;trade; open, secure runtime software&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform-a-reference-for-continuous-in-silicon-agent-monitoring/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Sentry reference design&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Findings are intended to inform safeguards across the wider computing ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p align="left"&gt;The commitment builds on NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s collaboration with the U.K.&amp;rsquo;s research community, including on the University of Bristol&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href="https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/isambard-ai/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Isambard-AI&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; supercomputer, powered by NVIDIA Grace Hopper Superchips.&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:03:46 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today announced a five-year compute donation valued at $250 million to strengthen the United Kingdom’s agentic safety and security research capability.]]></description><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-commits-250-million-to-advance-uk-agentic-safety-and-security-research-over-the-next-five-years</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:01:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>European Cities Deploy NVIDIA-Powered AI Agents to Run Smarter Urban Operations</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/european-cities-agents-urban-operations/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/af99a5398b196a1a4eca380e548b0b20/6acf1aa43d6332373f7a92ba_gtc-berlin-smart-cities-blog-842x450/gtc-berlin-smart-cities-blog-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=04cdaffa-6cb8-4d97-b22b-f0511e272af3" fileSize="134134" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/af99a5398b196a1a4eca380e548b0b20/6acf1aa43d6332373f7a92ba_gtc-berlin-smart-cities-blog-842x450/gtc-berlin-smart-cities-blog-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=04cdaffa-6cb8-4d97-b22b-f0511e272af3" alt="gtc-berlin-smart-cities-blog-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:01:12 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Keeping a city running means making decisions that affect residents every day — from when to repair a road to how to use energy more efficiently. Across the EMEA region, cities and local software, infrastructure and integration partners are using NVIDIA accelerated computing to build physical AI agents and digital twins that help teams make […]]]></description><author>Charbel Aoun</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/european-cities-agents-urban-operations/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:00:28 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>All Systems Go: Global PC App Ecosystem Ready for NVIDIA RTX Spark</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-laptops-software-updates/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bbc6b9cdf14fbe5f7664f977c0ea5447/6ace1dde3d63325cfcf07f50_nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=3d8579af-d065-4e3d-8444-5cd8f6dbb823" fileSize="54806" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bbc6b9cdf14fbe5f7664f977c0ea5447/6ace1dde3d63325cfcf07f50_nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=3d8579af-d065-4e3d-8444-5cd8f6dbb823" alt="nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:02:42 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA RTX Spark is a new beginning for the PC — a reinvention combining the capabilities of a gaming PC, a creative studio and a personal AI supercomputer into a single superchip. With up to 128GB of unified memory and 1 petaflop of AI compute, RTX Spark delivers the full stack of NVIDIA RTX and […]]]></description><author>Gerardo Delgado</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-laptops-software-updates/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:49 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Lands in Europe for GTC Berlin</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/gtc-berlin-2026-news/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/576359a162f64f9983d9b3de77530626/6acdbe983d633269055dc501_france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338/france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338_thmb.jpg?v=e3a43c90-678d-4e4d-b18a-856b0f5a0df1" fileSize="573324" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/576359a162f64f9983d9b3de77530626/6acdbe983d633269055dc501_france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338/france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338_thmb.jpg?v=e3a43c90-678d-4e4d-b18a-856b0f5a0df1" alt="france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:21:42 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA is in Europe, showcasing the future of technology together with the region’s developers, researchers and industry leaders.]]></description><author>NVIDIA Writers</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/gtc-berlin-2026-news/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:13:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>From Earth to Orbit, France’s Ecosystem Delivers Agentic Computing at Scale With NVIDIA</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/france-ecosystem-agentic-computing/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/f62fea35eec4b9278b81b95a5670bff3/6acdbb0e3d63327665b4e82e_france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450/france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=f8e7dd8e-6113-46c6-bc47-ab9f7abd3a0d" fileSize="15204" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/f62fea35eec4b9278b81b95a5670bff3/6acdbb0e3d63327665b4e82e_france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450/france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=f8e7dd8e-6113-46c6-bc47-ab9f7abd3a0d" alt="france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:01:05 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Companies in France are deploying agentic computing across industries spanning space, financial services, the public sector and scientific research, demonstrating how the country’s ecosystem has moved from ambition to application.  France’s progress sits on deliberate groundwork.  The AI Action Summit in February 2025 and Choose France Summits in 2025 and 2026 anchored major compute commitments […]]]></description><author>Nat Ives</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/france-ecosystem-agentic-computing/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:00:31 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>OCP Global Summit: Amid Ecosystem Adoption, NVIDIA Opens Vera Rubin Architecture to Help Scale AI Factories Worldwide</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ocp-global-summit-vera-rubin-scale-ai-factories/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/b714aa393d1a3d790925deb8cbedf198/6accf62c3d6332b0a1302305_gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450/gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=153b22de-a263-454a-98d0-56e9978185ba" fileSize="128393" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/b714aa393d1a3d790925deb8cbedf198/6accf62c3d6332b0a1302305_gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450/gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=153b22de-a263-454a-98d0-56e9978185ba" alt="gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:01:04 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[As AI factories grow from megawatts to gigawatts, building them takes more than advanced computing. Open standards are helping the industry scale AI infrastructure faster, more efficiently and more reliably. At the Open Compute Project (OCP) Global Summit, taking place in the San Jose McEnery Convention Center, NVIDIA announced new partnerships and contributions aimed at […]]]></description><author>NVIDIA Writers</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ocp-global-summit-vera-rubin-scale-ai-factories/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:25 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA and Cisco Introduce New Pluggable Optics Form Factor to Scale AI Factories</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-and-cisco-introduce-new-pluggable-optics-form-factor-to-scale-ai-factories</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bb0658e6668adfadaaf0477f22795d99/6acb0cef3d63325ab15dc4ff_ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable/ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable_thmb.jpg?v=6511e202-6a08-4834-996a-ced5c6faeac3" fileSize="320326" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bb0658e6668adfadaaf0477f22795d99/6acb0cef3d63325ab15dc4ff_ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable/ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable_thmb.jpg?v=6511e202-6a08-4834-996a-ced5c6faeac3" alt="Ultra-Dense Small Factor Pluggable" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle>New Transceivers Enable AI Builders to Scale Compute Within the Same Network Footprint While Reducing Networking’s Share of the Power Budget</subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-top:0in; margin-bottom:0.0001pt;"&gt;Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP) is designed to be the first module to support 400Gb/s-per-lane electrical signals, enabling capacity up to 12.8Tb/s so AI factory builders can scale Ethernet AI fabrics, while extending a proven deployment model across multiple generations of data center networks.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-top:0in; margin-bottom:0.0001pt;"&gt;USFP delivers 4x the bandwidth density and 1.3x the power efficiency of 200Gb/s-per-lane optics so AI factories can connect more computing systems without adding network tiers, while using less power to move each bit of data.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-top:0in; margin-bottom:0.0001pt;"&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco are working with TE Connectivity and Amphenol to build a multi-source hardware ecosystem around USFP.&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco today announced plans for Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP), a new high-density 400Gb/s-per-lane optical module designed to equip the hardware ecosystem for the next generation of AI factories using pluggable transceivers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As AI models grow and inference demand expands, AI factories must connect more computing systems while managing network complexity, power and costs. Moving more data per watt and per switch helps operators make better use of their infrastructure investments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scaling AI factories requires more bandwidth per connection and more connections per switch. When a switch reaches its capacity, further network expansion can require additional switch layers and optical links, increasing latency, power consumption and costs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;USFP is designed to enable AI factory builders to scale from 200 Gb/s per lane to 400Gb/s-per-lane Ethernet AI fabrics, while extending a deployment model proven at scale across multiple generations of data center networks. With USFP, customers can embrace next-generation optical technology and meet the performance demand of AI workloads without overhauling their data center infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first planned USFP-based transceivers will pack 16 full-duplex lanes in an octal small form factor (OSFP)-sized footprint supporting both switches and SuperNICs, with the ability to expand to 32 and more lanes in the future. By doubling both the lane count and bandwidth per lane, USFP enables AI fabrics to connect more 1.6Tb/s endpoints without adding network tiers. Customers will be able to achieve 12.8Tb/s of overall capacity with USFP.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Comparable with an OSFP-sized module, it delivers 4x the bandwidth and front-panel bandwidth density, with approximately 1.3x the power efficiency, versus 200Gb/s-per-lane pluggable modules. This means AI builders can increase their compute scale within the same network footprint, while decreasing networking&amp;rsquo;s share of the overall AI factory power budget.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Building the world&amp;rsquo;s largest AI factories starts with rethinking the smallest of connections,&amp;rdquo; said Gilad Shainer, senior vice president NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;With USFP, NVIDIA and Cisco are building an ecosystem to reinvent pluggable optics &amp;mdash; connecting more computing with greater efficiency to power the next generation of AI factories.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;AI builders need an interconnect architecture that can scale performance without locking them into a more complex operating model,&amp;rdquo; said Bill Gartner, senior vice president and general manager of optical systems and optics at Cisco. &amp;ldquo;Cisco and NVIDIA recognized that scaling pluggable optics to 400Gb/s per lane would require more than another incremental extension of today&amp;rsquo;s module designs. Through our collaboration, USFP is designed to deliver a new level of bandwidth density while preserving the serviceability, deployment flexibility and operational simplicity of pluggable optics. By taking a full-stack approach &amp;mdash; from silicon and systems to optics and the network operating system &amp;mdash; we can optimize every layer to deliver the performance and scale the next generation of AI networks will require.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More AI Infrastructure From Every Switch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Designed for electrical signals of 400Gb/s per lane, USFP uses a new two-dimensional array connector with a two-step insertion design that engages high-speed contacts after the module is inserted, reducing contact wear, improving signal integrity and making insertion force more predictable. The connector technology allows for further scaling of lane count to 32 full duplex lanes and more in the future. Because the connector is designed for 400Gb/s performance, it also offers improved performance at 200Gb/s per lane.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;USFP supports power dissipation of up to 100 watts without needing a separate, dedicated embedded cooling circuit within the transceiver, reducing switch design complexity and improving reliability. Together, these capabilities enable higher-bandwidth fabrics while preserving the mature deployment, serviceability and manufacturability of existing pluggable transceivers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All USFP configurations support optical designs that reduce latency and power consumption by simplifying signal processing. Support for a broad range of optical technologies and connection distances gives system designers the flexibility to meet unique AI factory deployment needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Hardware Ecosystem for Next-Generation AI Factories&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
NVIDIA and Cisco are collaborating with TE Connectivity and Amphenol to build USFP cages, connectors and modules, with additional partners expected to join. The shared form factor gives suppliers a common foundation for developing high-density pluggable infrastructure for 400Gb/s-per-lane fabrics to build a robust ecosystem for AI factory builders.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The collaboration builds on &lt;a href="https://newsroom.cisco.com/c/r/newsroom/en/us/a/y2026/m08/cisco-secure-ai-factory-nvidia-rack-scale.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title="NVIDIA and Cisco’s existing work"&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco&amp;rsquo;s existing work&lt;/a&gt; to ensure NVIDIA Spectrum-X&amp;trade; Ethernet networking and Cisco Silicon One-based Ethernet networks work together seamlessly, simplifying AI infrastructure deployment for enterprises, neoclouds and sovereign clouds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco plan to create an open industry specification for USFP through an upcoming community-led multi-source project.&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:05:42 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA and Cisco today announced plans for Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP), a new high-density 400Gb/s-per-lane optical module designed to equip the hardware ecosystem for the next generation of AI factories using pluggable transceivers.]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bb0658e6668adfadaaf0477f22795d99/ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable.jpg" length="320326" type="image/jpeg"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-and-cisco-introduce-new-pluggable-optics-form-factor-to-scale-ai-factories</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Into the Omniverse: How Developers Turn Ideas Into Simulations With Frontier AI Agents</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/developers-simulations-frontier-ai-agents/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/016b788b2d35ad703c42051807c2a4f2/6ac805fa3d63329b7859cf27_omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1/omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1_thmb.jpg?v=fa6d3afa-3fb1-41a9-a244-d472dfcb6b55" fileSize="20074565" type="video/mp4"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/016b788b2d35ad703c42051807c2a4f2/6ac805fa3d63329b7859cf27_omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1/omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1_thmb.jpg?v=fa6d3afa-3fb1-41a9-a244-d472dfcb6b55" alt="omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:07:09 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Turning a simulation idea into a working application means assembling assets, connecting physics and rendering, and checking that the scene behaves as intended. Developers are combining frontier AI models with NVIDIA Omniverse libraries to help carry out that work — building applications for exploring scenarios, investigating failures and improving designs. Developers direct AI agents through […]]]></description><author>NVIDIA Writers</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/developers-simulations-frontier-ai-agents/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:06:35 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Commits $1 Billion to Advance US Science Over the Next Five Years</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-commits-1-billion-to-advance-us-science-over-the-next-five-years</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" fileSize="5094489" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" alt="NVIDIA Voyager" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle>Commitments Will Strengthen Fields Critical for US Leadership Including Quantum Computing, Healthcare and Energy Security</subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type="disc"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NVIDIA announces commitments valued at $1 billion to advance U.S. science over the next five years, at a Washington event convening U.S. officials, industry leaders and members of the science community.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This builds on longstanding collaboration between NVIDIA and national labs, spanning two decades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA today announced commitments valued at $1 billion to build out the United States&amp;rsquo; capacity for super intelligence research and development in fields critical for U.S. leadership, including quantum computing, healthcare and energy security.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The announcement was made during the Science: A New Golden Age event in Washington, D.C., where U.S. officials, industry leaders and members of the science community convened on the public-private collaborations needed to bolster scientific exploration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;President Trump&amp;rsquo;s Genesis Mission is launching a new golden age of American discovery,&amp;rdquo; said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;With a $1 billion investment, NVIDIA is putting advanced Super Intelligence in the hands of America&amp;rsquo;s scientists to accelerate breakthroughs in medicine, energy and materials. This is how America turns scientific leadership into industrial leadership, and innovation into jobs and opportunity for generations.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During the event, the U.S. Office of Science and Technology Policy celebrated the expansion of the Genesis Mission, of which NVIDIA is a leading industry partner. In response, NVIDIA has invited members of the science community to collaborate in R&amp;amp;D using compute and super intelligence infrastructure resources to accelerate scientific discovery and promote U.S. innovation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthening US Leadership in Scientific Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Over the next five years, NVIDIA will commit $1 billion to the advancement of super intelligence for science and quantum computing across the U.S. through support of the nation&amp;rsquo;s higher-education research institutions, investments in accelerating American quantum leadership and support for cloud service providers bolstering U.S. government mission needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA is also a collaborator on a number of the phase 2 Genesis Mission awards announced today at the event, including projects in quantum computing, fusion, accelerator design and microelectronics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA has collaborated with U.S. national labs for more than two decades. Last year, it announced its partnership with the U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) on the Genesis Mission, which includes &lt;a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-oracle-us-department-of-energy-ai-supercomputer-scientific-discovery" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s work to build the department&amp;rsquo;s largest supercomputer for scientific research&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; at Argonne National Laboratory. This is in addition to supporting &lt;a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-partners-ai-infrastructure-america" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;seven new systems&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; across Argonne and Los Alamos National Laboratories, accelerating the DOE&amp;rsquo;s mission of driving technological leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:35:20 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today announced commitments valued at $1 billion to build out the United States’ capacity for super intelligence research and development in fields critical for U.S. leadership, including quantum computing, healthcare and energy security.]]></description><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-commits-1-billion-to-advance-us-science-over-the-next-five-years</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:31:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Rally Up: ‘Gears of War: E-Day’ Launches on GeForce NOW</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-gears-of-war-e-day/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/14fc8824076bdbffd0180b4d98e2a79b/6ac794223d6332663e580326_gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450/gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7dd5c271-5882-4cc5-9a64-7cb2b537e175" fileSize="92094" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/14fc8824076bdbffd0180b4d98e2a79b/6ac794223d6332663e580326_gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450/gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7dd5c271-5882-4cc5-9a64-7cb2b537e175" alt="gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:01:25 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Gears of War: E-Day leads the charge on GeForce NOW this week, bringing Marcus Fenix and Dom Santiago’s first fight against the Locust Horde to the cloud with GeForce RTX-powered performance. A new way to join the action is also coming: Fire TV users will soon be able to purchase GeForce NOW memberships directly through […]]]></description><author>GeForce NOW Community</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-gears-of-war-e-day/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:00:46 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA, Microsoft Kick Off a New Beginning for Windows PCs with RTX Spark and AI Agents</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-microsoft-windows-event/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202111/618c4510ed6ae54e51b85162_nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7f16f52c-ffb3-4f7e-a25d-61580f0dc38c" fileSize="75869" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202111/618c4510ed6ae54e51b85162_nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7f16f52c-ffb3-4f7e-a25d-61580f0dc38c" alt="nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:45:18 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[At a Microsoft event in San Francisco on Wednesday, Jensen Huang and Satya Nadella outlined how NVIDIA and Microsoft are co-engineering hardware and software for AI agents to run on Windows PCs. NVIDIA was founded because of Windows, Huang said. Now AI agents are coming to Windows. “If you look at the entire journey of […]]]></description><author>Gerardo Delgado</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-microsoft-windows-event/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:45:28 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>